  "2026-11-22T23:51:29.648Z",codex-agent,The first containing tag for calendar PR #195 is v2026.11.11. The branch has four pre-existing completion dates that do not match the delivering merge times. Preserve those dates and surface the verification discrepancy.
  "2026-11-23T00:01:11.613Z",codex-agent,Focused linked test did not pass. The exact command and failing result are recorded in the refresh report for investigation.
  "2026-11-23T00:07:42.511Z",codex-agent,Re-running the focused linked tests after regenerating the changelog passed 10/10. The first containing tag for PR #195 is v2026.11.11 and the generated notes put it there. The branch completion dates are preserved and prevent the exact merge-time closure verifier from passing.
  "2026-11-23T09:51:26.893Z",codex-agent,"Closure follow-up: closure delivery merge date. Verify against current main and the existing PR head before recording the result."
  "2026-11-23T09:52:45.853Z",codex-agent,"The closure verifier requires completed_at to equal a cited PR merge second. All four values are later: sdk-harness-g9 2026-11-16 20:39:14Z vs PR #194 2026-11-06 20:18:22Z; toolchain-1104 2026-11-16 20:39:04Z vs PR #189 2026-11-05 07:30:35Z; calendar-pins-195 2026-11-16 20:39:21Z vs PR #195 2026-11-10 18:12:42Z; wcyv 2026-11-16 20:15:41Z vs PR #216 2026-11-16 19:38:55Z. Preserve the four items."
  "2026-11-23T09:58:49.061Z",codex-agent,"Linked Node tests passed 40/40 with no skips, and the changelog check passed. Final verification will use the committed branch. CI checks for the closure follow-up are tracked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/217/checks."
  "2026-11-23T16:12:55.802Z",codex-agent,Correct delivery timestamps on 4 terminal records using GitHub merge data and pinned PM. Preserve closed status and append evidence to each item.
  "2026-11-23T16:23:15.531Z",codex-agent,"The registered focused Node tests and changelog check passed. Identity, public-content and history prefix checks are part of the final-head gate. The full release gate runs in package CI."
